do
---An [upgrade planner](https://wiki.factorio.com/Upgrade_planner).
---
---For an entity to be allowed as an upgrade source, it must be minable, may not have "not-upgradable" flag set and may not be [hidden](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/PrototypeBase.html%23hidden#hidden). Additionally, the source entity's mining result must not be an item product that is [hidden](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html%23hidden#hidden). Mining results with no item products are allowed.
---
---For an entity to be allowed as an upgrade target, it must have least 1 item that builds it that isn't hidden.
---
---For two entities to be upgrades of each other, the two entities must have the same [fast replaceable group](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html%23fast_replaceable_group#fast_replaceable_group), the same [collision box](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html%23collision_box#collision_box) and the same [collision mask](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html%23collision_mask#collision_mask). Additionally, [underground belts](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/UndergroundBeltPrototype.html) cannot be upgraded to [transport belts](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TransportBeltPrototype.html) and vice versa.
---
---For an entity to be automatically upgraded to another entity without configuring the upgrade planner, the [next upgrade](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html%23next_upgrade#next_upgrade) of the upgrade source entity must be set.
---
